 "chunks": [
  {
   "text": "When sigma is one or less, the arrows don't shrink fast enough,",
   "start": 0.7,
   "end": 4.175
  },
  {
   "text": "and the sum never settles.",
   "start": 4.175,
   "end": 5.963
  },
  {
   "text": "Think of one, plus x, plus x squared, and so on.",
   "start": 5.963,
   "end": 9.775
  },
  {
   "text": "It only works between minus one and one,",
   "start": 9.775,
   "end": 12.25
  },
  {
   "text": "but it clearly wants to be one over one minus x,",
   "start": 12.25,
   "end": 15.3
  },
  {
   "text": "which makes sense almost everywhere.",
   "start": 15.3,
   "end": 17.55
  },
  {
   "text": "In the same way, zeta has exactly one smooth extension to the whole complex plane,",
   "start": 18.5,
   "end": 23.712
  },
  {
   "text": "except the point s equals one.",
   "start": 23.712,
   "end": 26.038
  },
  {
   "text": "Here it is.",
   "start": 26.038,
   "end": 27.188
  },
  {
   "text": "Color shows the direction of zeta's value, and each ring doubles its size.",
   "start": 27.188,
   "end": 31.95
  },
  {
   "text": "Where all the colors meet, zeta is zero.",
   "start": 31.95,
   "end": 34.75
  }
 ],
